osx-gpu: read the extension flags as the bytes they are

_mesa_extension_supported() reads struct gl_extensions, whose members are
GLboolean (one byte), through a pointer to bool. On 32-bit Darwin PowerPC
bool has four bytes, so flag n was looked for at byte 4n: the list of
extensions a program got (glGetString, glGetStringi, GL_NUM_EXTENSIONS) had
14 the context lacks and lacked 87 it has, GL_ARB_vertex_program among
them. Mesa's own decisions were not affected: they ask each flag by name.

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/extensions.c b/src/mesa/main/extensions.c
--- a/src/mesa/main/extensions.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/extensions.c
@@ -316,7 +316,10 @@
 static inline bool
 _mesa_extension_supported(const struct gl_context *ctx, extension_index i)
 {
-   const bool *base = (bool *) &ctx->Extensions;
+   /* GLboolean, as the members of struct gl_extensions are, not bool:
+    * bool has four bytes on 32-bit Darwin PowerPC, and the offset is in
+    * bytes. */
+   const GLboolean *base = (const GLboolean *) &ctx->Extensions;
    const struct mesa_extension *ext = _mesa_extension_table + i;
 
    return (ctx->Version >= ext->version[ctx->API]) && base[ext->offset];
